ries, or package-health damage.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8adf8a2e66a94831","cmd-35c0fbc2bf234af4","cmd-20a37f3b3c4f47b1","cmd-8db39bb71c2240a5","cmd-3d5a7bb189824156","cmd-af4b35d8c9814fc4","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes are satisfied. The evidence directly demonstrates creation and mounting of the logical volume, uninterrupted online growth to 2.00 GiB with content integrity, retention of the installed OS and kernel, and persistence across a completed node restart. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete: healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement and observed disconnect, changed boot identity, and recovered read-write storage are all captured and independently corroborated by lifecycle boot identities.","limitations":[]}
